    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 19 February 2007, proposal to build a single storey rear extension measuring 7.25 metres wide, 3.15 metres deep from the rear of the house and 3.00 metres high, and 4.00m high where indicated on the approved plans when measured externally was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe development is within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume of the extension is less than 10% the volume of the original house.\r\n"
